have the video footage. The way that people were dressed as they come off the boat in those pictures is significant, particularly if you come from this tradition, because what they are dressed in is what people used to call Sunday best. The women wear gloves, they wear hats. The men wear suits and ties with tie pins, and they also wear hats. The background that I come from, that's what you do if you're going to church. And if you're wearing these clothes, it's because it's an important moment and you're going to share something valuable, something significant in your life. It's not like we do these days, you know, get on a plane in your T-shirt and jeans. And if you're going somewhere important, you'll dress when you get there. I remember actually I was born in London, but as a child, shuffled a bit back and forth. I remember on one occasion
视频片段，那是不可能奏效的。人们在那些照片中下船时的着装方式意义重大，特别是如果你来自这个传统，因为他们穿的是人们过去常说的“周日最佳”（Sunday best）。女性戴着手套，戴着帽子。男性穿着西装，打着领带，戴着领带夹，也戴着帽子。在我成长的背景中，如果你要去教堂，你就会这样做。如果你穿着这些衣服，那是因为这是一个重要的时刻，你要去分享生活中宝贵、重要的事情。不像我们现在这样，你知道，穿着 T 恤和牛仔裤上飞机。如果你要去重要的地方，你会在到达后再换装。我记得实际上我出生在伦敦，但小时候来回搬迁。我记得有一次

