I think it is very unusual in this world to be a person who can claim more than one cultural and ethnic tradition completely as your own. And I don't know how that feels. Most of us don't know how that feels. And most people in the world do not know how that feels. And I think that's a fantastic thing. I think it's a huge advantage. It's like being bilingual only on steroids. And I think these are very, very special people. But how we deal with it and how they deal with it, we don't know yet. And it's still to be seen. I would love to see more writing, more history about this phenomenon than there currently is, because it's special, and we need to understand
我认为在这个世界上，能够完全声称拥有不止一种文化和民族传统的人是非常不寻常的。我不知道那是什么感觉。我们大多数人不知道那是什么感觉。世界上大多数人不知道那是什么感觉。我认为这是一件美妙的事情。我认为这是一个巨大的优势。这就像双语，只是加强版。我认为这些人非常、非常特别。但我们如何处理它，他们如何处理它，我们还不知道。这还有待观察。我很乐意看到更多关于这种现象的写作和历史，而不是目前的情况，因为它是特殊的，我们需要理解

